// Sidebar look "rex" (`sidebar.look`): the sidebar drawn like Rex's, a plain list of sessions.
// Every value here is an ordinary public sidebar setting. It fills only the keys that your
// cmux-next.json, a theme file and managed settings leave unset, so your own settings still win.
// To make your own, copy these lines into ~/.config/cmux/cmux-next.json and edit them.
//
// From the reference (docs/cmux-next/sidebar-customization.md, "Sidebar looks"; the Minimal sessions
// theme file, Resources/theme-files/minimal-sessions.json, is the same list with its density too):
// - One flat list of sessions: no folders, headings or counts.
// - The status leads the row, in the icon's place: a spinner while it works, its own mark when it is
//   blocked, done or failed, nothing when idle. The row keeps that slot while idle, so the name never
//   moves when work starts or stops.
// - Then the name: no icon, color or time.
// The look never sets row height, sidebar width, the trailing column or motion: those stay on
// cmux's shared grid (`sidebar.density`, `appearance.metrics.*`), so switching looks moves no pane.
{
  "name": "Rex",
  "description": "One flat list of sessions: the status first, then the name.",

  "sidebar.groupBy": "none",
  "sidebar.groupHeader.memberCount": false,
  "sidebar.groupHeader.unreadCount": false,

  "sidebar.workspaceRow.statusPlacement": "leading",
  "sidebar.detailedStatusIcons": true,

  "sidebar.workspaceRow.icon": false,
  "sidebar.showColors": false,
  "sidebar.showTimestamps": false
}
